{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-3b2a8ff9-0743-4db3-9ed0-1561d1a0929a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc61efddf22bf3f2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-9kjmo_fl/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8009: Workspace-aware artifact serving for multi-tenant MLflow deployments\n\nStrategy effort M-L (4-7 sprints), three strategy components (MLflow, MLflow Operator,\nmlflow-kubernetes-plugins), one team (MLflow Team). Triage (Step 0): not below threshold\n(M-L scope spanning three architecturally distinct sub-systems — server flag composition,\noperator split-server topology, plugin workspace resolution — that warrant separate PR\nreview cycles); not documentation-only (active code changes in all three components).\nProceeded to full decomposition.\n\n## Staff Engineer Input Overrides (Step 1.5)\n\nThe Staff Engineer / SME Input section is non-empty and takes precedence. Three directives,\nall reflected in the epic scopes:\n\n1. **No new flag — combine existing flags.** No epic introduces `--artifacts-only-workspace-aware`\n   or a `spec.artifactsOnly.workspaceAware` CR field. The server epic composes the existing\n   `--artifacts-only` and `--enable-workspaces` flags; the operator epic propagates existing\n   workspace configuration to the artifacts-only instance. (The strategy body already\n   incorporates this correction; the decomposition enforces it as an acceptance criterion on\n   both the plugin and server epics.)\n2. **Operator work is a split deployment, not a config toggle.** The operator epic delivers a\n   dedicated artifacts-only Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute plus artifact\n   traffic routing from the main tracking deployment — a split-server topology. No epic\n   treats this as a single CR-field toggle.\n3. **SSAR detail is over-specified.** Epics state that workspace authorization reuses the\n   existing auth plugin infrastructure without dictating Kubernetes API mechanics\n   (SelfSubjectAccessReview against `mlflow.kubeflow.org` pseudo-resources is removed from\n   all epic scopes). The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup are\n   unchanged.\n\n## Component Mappings (canonical Jira component vocabulary)\n\n`.context/rhai-components.txt` has no canonical entries for \"MLflow Operator\" or\n\"mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\". Every epic carries the closest canonical name **MLflow**:\n\n| Strategy component | Canonical component | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| MLflow | MLflow | exact match |\n| MLflow Operator | MLflow | no canonical \"MLflow Operator\"; closest canonical name is MLflow |\n| mlflow-kubernetes-plugins | MLflow | no canonical entry; plugin is part of the MLflow serving surface |\n\nAll epic `component` frontmatter values are `MLflow`; the per-epic spans are visible in the\nEpic List below. `submit.py` would silently strip any non-canonical name, so this mapping is\nload-bearing for Jira labeling.\n\n## Open Question and Assumption Disposition\n\n| Strategy unknown | Disposition |\n|---|---|\n| Does workspace store / plugin initialization depend on tracking store availability? (OQ, MLflow Team) | **Investigation E001** — gates the plugin and server epics (`rewrite`): the answer determines verify-and-extend vs. refactor into an independent initialization path. |\n| How should the operator configure artifact traffic routing, and does the tracking server need a config change? (OQ, MLflow Team) | **Investigation E004** — gates the operator epic (`rewrite`); bounded outcomes produce conditional branch `BRANCH-B-E009` (server-side delegation config) if required. |\n| Artifact request paths carry sufficient information to resolve workspace membership? (assumption, needs validation) | Folded into **E001** (feasibility under the standard S3 artifact store configuration) and **E002** (adversarial/malformed paths must be denied). |\n| Helm chart rendering supports a second Deployment without structural changes? (assumption, needs validation) | Acceptance criterion on the operator epic E007 — the epic exists and proceeds identically either way (failure = fix within the epic). |\n| `--artifacts-only` composable with `--enable-workspaces` without breaking either flag individually? (assumption, needs validation) | Acceptance criterion on the server epic E006 (backwards-compatibility ACs; failure = fix within the epic). The epic's deliverable is the composability itself. |\n| Single-tenant deployments do not set `--enable-workspaces`? (assumption, needs validation) | Acceptance criterion on E006 and regression scenario in E008. |\n| Acceptable latency overhead per artifact request? (OQ, PM/Engineering) | **Non-gating** — product decision; captured as a measure-then-optimize AC on E006 (short-TTL caching if the agreed target is exceeded, per the strategy's risk mitigation). No epic's existence or approach changes. |\n| Audit telemetry channel for workspace denials? (OQ, PM/Security) | **Non-gating** — HLR-8 already commits to server logs; captured as an AC on E006. If PM/Security later selects a different channel (OTLP, K8s audit log), scope extends additively — see Health Warnings. |\n\n**Safety-critical handling (Rule 19):** this strategy enforces tenant-boundary authorization\n(workspace-membership access control with a fail-closed mandate) — an RBAC-class security\nmechanism. Rule 19 therefore generates a security Investigation (E002, bypass vectors) and a\nfail-mode Investigation (E003, fail-closed confirmation), both blocking the main server\nimplementation; E002 also blocks the operator epic (misconfiguration bypass).\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Component (canonical) | Team | Priority |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| E001 | Validate workspace resolution dependencies in the artifacts-only server context | Investigation | MLflow (mlflow-kubernetes-plugins + MLflow server init) | MLflow Team | P0 |\n| E002 | Security analysis: bypass vectors for workspace-aware artifact serving | Investigation | MLflow | MLflow Team | P0 |\n| E003 | Failure-mode analysis for fail-closed workspace-aware artifact serving | Investigation | MLflow | MLflow Team | P0 |\n| E004 | Determine artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology | Investigation | MLflow (MLflow Operator) | MLflow Team | P1 |\n| E005 | Extend mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only context | Implementation | MLflow (mlflow-kubernetes-plugins) | MLflow Team | P0 |\n| E006 | Workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow tracking server | Implementation | MLflow | MLflow Team | P0 |\n| E007 | MLflow operator split-server topology for workspace-aware artifact serving | Implementation | MLflow (MLflow Operator) | MLflow Team | P1 |\n| E008 | Integration validation of workspace-aware artifact serving across the split-server topology | Implementation | MLflow | MLflow Team | P1 |\n| BRANCH-B-E009 | Main tracking server artifact-traffic delegation configuration (branch B) | Implementation | MLflow | MLflow Team | P1 |\n\nEpic count: 8 main-plan epics plus 1 conditional branch epic. Branch epics are excluded from\nthe main-plan critical path.\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 Workspace resolution dependencies (Inv)\"] --> E005[\"E005 Plugin workspace resolution (Impl)\"]\n    E001 --> E006[\"E006 Server workspace-aware artifacts-only serving (Impl)\"]\n    E002[\"E002 Security bypass analysis (Inv)\"] --> E005\n    E002 --> E006\n    E002 --> E007[\"E007 Operator split-server topology (Impl)\"]\n    E003[\"E003 Failure-mode analysis (Inv)\"] --> E006\n    E004[\"E004 Routing design (Inv)\"] --> E007\n    E004 --> E009B[\"BRANCH-B-E009 Server delegation config (branch)\"]\n    E005 --> E006\n    E005 --> E008[\"E008 Integration validation (Impl)\"]\n    E006 --> E008