{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-81cd17a1-788b-4e88-bd2d-9d9b2aa9647e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd46218bda44861a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-9kjmo_fl/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E001.md","content":"# Validate workspace resolution dependencies in the artifacts-only server context\n\n## Description\n\nInvestigation resolving whether the existing workspace resolution machinery — the\n`mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin (registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider`\nentry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) and the `kubernetes://` workspace\nstore — can initialize and resolve experiment-to-workspace mapping in an MLflow server\nrunning with `--artifacts-only`, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not\ninitialized. The strategy flags this as an open question (\"Does the workspace store\ninitialization in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins depend on tracking store availability?\") and\nmarks the related assumptions as needing validation. The answer determines whether the plugin\nwork is a verification-and-extension or a refactoring of workspace resolution into an\nindependent initialization path, and shapes the server's workspace-provider initialization.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Analyze the initialization path of the `kubernetes-auth` workspace provider and determine,\n  with code-level evidence, whether its initialization (and the `kubernetes://` workspace\n  store it backs) depends on tracking store or model registry store initialization.\n- Determine whether experiment-to-workspace mapping is obtainable from the `kubernetes://`\n  workspace store without initialized tracking stores.\n- Analyze artifact request paths handled by the artifacts-only proxy under the standard S3\n  artifact store configuration (artifact paths follow the `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`\n  structure) and confirm whether they carry sufficient information (experiment ID or run ID)\n  to resolve workspace membership; document how paths that do not resolve must be treated.\n- Confirm that `--artifacts-only` and `--enable-workspaces` can be made composable without\n  breaking the server initialization sequence for either flag used individually.\n- Document limitations for non-standard artifact roots (initial implementation is scoped to\n  the S3 artifact store per the strategy's risk mitigation).\n- Produce a findings document with a recommended approach — verification only, or refactoring\n  workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin — sufficient\n  to scope the plugin and server implementation work without further investigation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The findings document states, with code-level evidence, whether workspace provider and\n  workspace store initialization depends on tracking store availability; if coupled, the\n  specific coupling points and the refactoring needed to decouple them are identified.\n- The findings document states with a concrete pass/fail whether experiment-to-workspace\n  mapping is obtainable from the `kubernetes://` workspace store without tracking store\n  initialization.\n- The findings document confirms or refutes, for the standard S3 artifact store\n  configuration, that artifact request paths contain the information needed to resolve\n  workspace membership, and specifies that unresolvable paths are denied rather than served.\n- The findings document records whether combining `--artifacts-only` with\n  `--enable-workspaces` breaks the initialization sequence of either flag used individually,\n  and if so, what sequence change is required.\n- A recommended implementation approach (verify-and-extend vs. refactor into an independent\n  initialization path) is recorded and is specific enough to scope the downstream\n  implementation work.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nInvestigation epic — no HLR ownership. De-risks HLR-1, HLR-2, and HLR-7 by determining\nwhether workspace validation can function at all in the artifacts-only server context.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The strategy's risk table directs this validation early (\"Validate the plugin's\n  initialization dependencies early in sprint 1\") — it gates both the plugin and server\n  implementation epics.\n- `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` has no dedicated architecture-context file; it is documented\n  indirectly by the MLflow architecture context as the external `kubernetes-auth` plugin\n  package (v1.5.0). The strategy's claims about its registration mechanism\n  (`mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group, `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) are not\n  corroborated by the context file and are part of what this investigation verifies.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":90628,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a71db037e41f9110","agent_id":"a42b59692a3812c5b","session_id":"36784e31-2123-4326-9e59-f3bb80327bfe","uuid":"e93b9d6d-1599-4f43-a23a-24bb827c3eb3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:40:53.868Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
