{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c505932f-a68c-4164-9360-33ff28f70329","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b71784cd7895730b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-9kjmo_fl/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E003.md","content":"# Failure-mode analysis for fail-closed workspace-aware artifact serving\n\n## Description\n\nInvestigation enumerating the failure modes of workspace-aware artifact serving and\nconfirming that the fail-closed posture covers each. The strategy specifies two modes\nexplicitly — the workspace store being unreachable (requests denied, HTTP 503) and\n`--enable-workspaces` being set without `--workspace-store-uri` (server fails to start with a\nclear error) — but the remaining modes are unspecified and determine the server's\nerror-handling behavior: per-request resolution errors, plugin exceptions mid-request, error\nvs. empty vs. partial responses from the workspace store, and timeout behavior. Because this\nstrategy enforces tenant isolation, every failure mode must be confirmed to fail closed\n(deny) rather than open (serve without validation).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enumerate failure modes across the request lifecycle:\n  - Startup: missing or misconfigured `--workspace-store-uri`, workspace provider/plugin load\n    failure.\n  - Per-request: workspace store unreachable, experiment-to-workspace resolution errors,\n    auth plugin exceptions mid-request, malformed or partial workspace store responses,\n    timeouts.\n- For each mode, define the required response consistent with the fail-closed mandate\n  (deny, never serve without validation) and the user-visible behavior (HTTP status and\n  error message), including the strategy-specified modes (503 with an indication that\n  workspace validation is unavailable; fail-to-start with a clear error).\n- Produce a failure-mode to response matrix that the server implementation adopts as its\n  error-handling acceptance criteria.\n- Identify any failure mode where the planned design would fail open, together with the\n  required design change.\n- If short-TTL caching of workspace membership decisions is introduced for latency, include\n  cache-unavailability and cache-staleness modes in the matrix.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The failure-mode to response matrix covers the startup and per-request modes listed above,\n  with a defined response for every mode.\n- Every runtime failure mode in the matrix denies the artifact request (fail-closed); any\n  mode where the planned design would fail open is identified together with a remediation\n  requirement.\n- The two strategy-specified modes are included and consistent with the strategy: workspace\n  store unreachable yields HTTP 503 indicating workspace validation is unavailable; startup\n  with workspace-aware artifacts-only mode and no explicit workspace store URI fails with a\n  clear error.\n- The matrix is specific enough to serve directly as the error-handling acceptance criteria\n  for the server implementation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nInvestigation epic — no HLR ownership. De-risks HLR-3 (fail-closed behavior) and HLR-2\n(denial semantics for requests that cannot be validated).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The strategy's Non-Functional Requirements mandate fail-closed behavior (\"Failure to\n  validate must result in access denial\"); this investigation turns that mandate into an\n  exhaustive, testable matrix rather than a two-case specification.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":92523,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a71db037e41f9110","agent_id":"a42b59692a3812c5b","session_id":"36784e31-2123-4326-9e59-f3bb80327bfe","uuid":"fa7debbb-9833-4504-ab8e-6714c51b86d5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:41:32.729Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
