{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e3f70dd9-45ce-4b69-a1a8-50d55d7d12fe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a11b35f00d5889d2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-9kjmo_fl/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E005.md","content":"# Extend mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only context\n\n## Description\n\nMakes the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin's workspace resolution function correctly\nin the MLflow artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores\nare not initialized. Depending on the outcome of the workspace-resolution dependency\ninvestigation, this is verification and extension of the existing resolution, or a\nrefactoring of workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the\nplugin. The plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking\nserver's non-artifact operations; this epic extends that capability to the artifacts-only\nproxy context.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Verify and, where needed, extend the plugin's workspace resolution so it initializes and\n  resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping without tracking store or model registry store\n  initialization.\n- If the workspace-resolution dependency investigation finds coupling to the full tracking\n  server initialization path: factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization\n  path within the plugin, preserving existing behavior for the full tracking server.\n- Apply the path-resolution and resolution-hardening requirements from the security bypass\n  analysis: unresolvable or ambiguous artifact paths must produce a deniable outcome, never\n  a silent or wrong-workspace mapping.\n- Preserve the existing registration mechanism (the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point\n  group loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) and the existing behavior for the tracking\n  server's non-artifact operations — changes to workspace isolation for non-artifact\n  operations are out of scope per the strategy.\n- Workspace authorization continues to reuse the existing auth plugin infrastructure; the\n  kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup are unchanged. Per Staff\n  Engineer input, Kubernetes API mechanics are implementation details and are not prescribed\n  at strategy level.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The plugin's workspace resolution initializes in a server context where tracking and model\n  registry stores are not initialized, demonstrated by a test reproducing the artifacts-only\n  initialization.\n- Experiment-to-workspace resolution returns correct mappings for resolvable artifact paths\n  and a safe denial outcome for unresolvable or malformed paths, per the security analysis\n  requirements.\n- The tracking server's existing non-artifact workspace resolution behavior is unchanged\n  (regression check).\n- No new server flag, CR field, or changed CLI argument is introduced by this work (Staff\n  Engineer input: no `--artifacts-only-workspace-aware` flag or equivalent).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1): Auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only\n  context without tracking store initialization.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Approach (verify-and-extend vs. refactor) is determined by the workspace-resolution\n  dependency investigation; if coupled, the refactoring is within this epic's scope.\n- The plugin has no dedicated architecture-context file; it is documented indirectly by the\n  MLflow architecture context as the external `kubernetes-auth` plugin package (v1.5.0).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":94094,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a71db037e41f9110","agent_id":"a42b59692a3812c5b","session_id":"36784e31-2123-4326-9e59-f3bb80327bfe","uuid":"c