{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-baa83b19-bf21-4f3d-92a3-a7a7755af5bc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa61cb85bbdb420e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-9kjmo_fl/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E007.md","content":"# MLflow operator split-server topology for workspace-aware artifact serving\n\n## Description\n\nExtends the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a\nseparate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — a split-server topology — and to\nconfigure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated\ninstance. This is a split deployment, not a single-deployment configuration toggle (Staff\nEngineer input). The operator propagates workspace configuration to the artifacts-only\ninstance using the same configuration mechanisms it already uses for the main tracking\ndeployment.\n\n## Scope\n\n- New Helm chart templates within the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (MLflow\n  CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, applied via\n  server-side apply) for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute.\n- Configuration of the main tracking deployment's artifact traffic routing to the dedicated\n  instance, per the mechanism selected by the artifact traffic routing design investigation\n  (ingress-level routing vs. server-side delegation; not prescribed here).\n- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`,\n  `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration\n  mechanisms as the main tracking deployment; the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar is deployed on the\n  artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment.\n- Gateway API HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance created conditionally\n  based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for\n  optional dependencies.\n- Operator validation that rejects split-server configurations where the artifacts-only\n  instance would lack workspace flags, so misconfiguration cannot result in artifact\n  requests bypassing workspace validation (strategy risk mitigation; requirements refined\n  by the security bypass analysis).\n- The split-server topology is opt-in: deployments that do not enable it retain the current\n  single-deployment topology (rollback path).\n- Verification that the operator's Helm chart rendering supports the additional Deployment\n  for the artifacts-only instance without structural changes to the chart architecture\n  (strategy assumption validated during implementation).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciliation creates a\n  dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main\n  tracking Deployment, measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the\n  correct flag combinations.\n- The dedicated artifacts-only Deployment's container command runs with `--artifacts-only\n  --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth\n  --serve-artifacts`, verified by inspecting the rendered Deployment spec.\n- Artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment is routed to the dedicated\n  artifacts-only instance per the selected routing design, verified end-to-end.\n- The operator rejects split-server configurations where the artifacts-only instance would\n  lack workspace flags, with a clear validation error.\n- Deployments that do not enable split-server artifact serving reconcile identically to\n  current behavior (no additional resources created; backwards compatible), providing the\n  rollback path.\n- Workspace configuration propagation to the artifacts-only instance uses the same\n  mechanisms as the main tracking deployment.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P1): operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment\n  with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n  artifacts-only instance. (If the routing design investigation selects server-side\n  delegation, the main-tracking-server portion of this HLR is planned in the conditional\n  branch of the decomposition.)\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The flag combination above requires the server-side flag composability delivered by the\n  workspace-aware artifacts-only serving work in the MLflow tracking server. This is a\n  configuration reference, not a build-against dependency: the operator templates are\n  developed in parallel, and the coupling is enforced by the rendered Deployment\n  verification above, never by a scheduling dependency.\n- Strategy assumption to validate during implementation: the Helm chart rendering supports\n  a second Deployment without structural changes to the chart architecture.\n- No new CR field semantics beyond what the strategy states; per Staff Engineer input, no\n  `spec.artifactsOnly.workspaceAware` field is introduced.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":96309,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a71db037e41f9110","agent_id":"a42b59692a3812c5b","session_id":"36784e31-2123-4326-9e59-f3bb80327bfe","uuid":"d7fb7a4b-6f2d-4c49-89e4-c3708e9f4b36","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:42:40.209Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
