{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f92c242e-2098-474d-bb1e-5aaa442896d8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a5f9a44daa8117a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-9kjmo_fl/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E008.md","content":"# Integration validation of workspace-aware artifact serving across the split-server topology\n\n## Description\n\nCross-component integration and regression validation of the strategy's scenarios once the\nserver, plugin, and operator work has landed, corresponding to the strategy's integration\ntesting budget: multi-tenant workspace scenarios, backwards compatibility and single-tenant\nregression, fail-closed edge cases, and split-server routing. The strategy's acceptance\ncriteria are end-to-end scenarios that span the deployed split-server topology, so they are\nverified here against the integrated system in addition to the per-epic acceptance\ncriteria.\n\n## Scope\n\n- End-to-end multi-tenant scenarios through the deployed split-server topology: a workspace\n  member is served artifacts of their workspace's experiments (HTTP 200 with correct\n  content); a non-member is denied (HTTP 403 with an insufficient-permissions error).\n- Fail-closed edge cases as deployed: workspace store unreachable yields HTTP 503\n  indicating workspace validation is unavailable, and every failure mode from the\n  failure-mode to response matrix denies rather than serves.\n- Single-tenant and non-workspace deployment regression: deployments without\n  `--enable-workspaces` retain current artifacts-only behavior.\n- Split-server routing verification: artifact traffic reaches the dedicated artifacts-only\n  instance; experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry operations remain on\n  the main tracking deployment.\n- Backwards compatibility of existing API contracts, CLI arguments, and configuration keys\n  (str