{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcc981061f6587ae","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n3\ttitle: Workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow tracking server\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n14\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: rewrite\n17\t  fallback_approach: If workspace resolution cannot be decoupled from tracking store\n18\t    initialization, the server's workspace-provider initialization approach is rewritten\n19\t    (the server may need to host a minimal resolution context rather than initializing\n20\t    only the workspace provider); security and fail-mode findings may add remediation\n21\t    scope to the request-handling path.\n22\tai_signals:\n23\t  change_specificity: 1\n24\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n25\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n26\t  existing_foundation: 1\n27\t  open_questions: -1\n28\t  external_dependency: 0\n29\t  human_process_gates: 0\n30\t  repo_access: 1\n31\t  architecture_claims: 1\n32\timplementation_type: null\n33\tinvestigation_signals: null\n34\tai_implementability: High\n35\tai_implementability_score: 5\n36\tjira_key: null\n37\tbranch: null\n38\t---\n39\t# Workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow tracking server\n40\t\n41\t## Description\n42\t\n43\tMakes `--artifacts-only` composable with `--enable-workspaces` in the MLflow tracking\n44\tserver. When both flags are set, the server requires an explicit `--workspace-store-uri`,\n45\tinitializes only the workspace provider needed to validate artifact requests, and validates\n46\tevery artifact request against workspace membership before serving. Tracking stores and\n47\tmodel registry stores stay uninitialized, and non-artifact API endpoints remain disabled.\n48\tNo new server flag is introduced — the workspace-aware behavior emerges from combining the\n49\texisting flags (Staff Engineer input). The design is fail-closed: if workspace validation\n50\tcannot be completed, artifact requests are denied rather than served without validation.\n51\t\n52\t## Scope\n53\t\n54\t- Flag composition: allow `--artifacts-only` to combine with `--enable-workspaces`; when\n55\t  combined, require an explicit `--workspace-store-uri` and fail to start with a clear error\n56\t  if it is absent.\n57\t- Initialize only the workspace provider needed to validate artifact requests; tracking\n58\t  stores and model registry stores remain uninitialized; non-artifact API endpoints remain\n59\t  disabled.\n60\t- Workspace validation of artifact requests: resolve the artifact path to its parent\n61\t  experiment (artifacts are stored under experiment-scoped paths), look up the experiment's\n62\t  workspace assignment via the workspace store, and delegate authorization to the existing\n63\t  auth plugin infrastructure. Requests failing workspace validation are denied with HTTP 403.\n64\t- Fail-closed error handling implementing the failure-mode to response matrix: every\n65\t  failure mode (workspace store unreachable, resolution errors, plugin exceptions, malformed\n66\t  or partial store responses, timeouts) denies the request — including HTTP 503 with an\n67\t  indication that workspace validation is unavailable when the workspace store is\n68\t  unreachable. No fail-open path.\n69\t- Backwards compatibility: `--artifacts-only` without `--enable-workspaces` retains current\n70\t  behavior; deployments that do not set `--enable-workspaces` are unaffected; no existing\n71\t  API contract, CLI argument, or configuration key changes meaning.\n72\t- Audit logging of workspace access denials through server logs, with sufficient context to\n73\t  audit (requesting identity, artifact path, workspace, outcome).\n74\t- Performance: measure the per-request latency overhead of workspace validation; if it\n75\t  exceeds the target agreed with PM/Engineering, implement short-TTL caching of workspace\n76\t  membership decisions consistent with caching patterns already used in the tracking\n77\t  server's auth path, honoring the security analysis's cache-staleness requirements.\n78\t- Document limitations for non-standard artifact roots (initial implementation scoped to\n79\t  the S3 artifact store, per the strategy's risk mitigation).\n80\t\n81\t## Acceptance Criteria\n82\t\n83\t- Given the artifacts-only instance started with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces\n84\t  --workspace-store-uri kubernetes://`, a user who is a member of workspace A requesting an\n85\t  artifact belonging to an experiment in workspace A is served successfully (HTTP 200 with\n86\t  correct artifact content).\n87\t- A user who is a member of workspace A but not workspace B requesting an artifact belonging\n88\t  to an experiment in workspace B is denied with HTTP 403 and an error message indicating\n89\t  insufficient workspace permissions.\n90\t- Given `--artifacts-only` set without `--enable-workspaces`, any authenticated user is\n91\t  served without workspace validation (current behavior preserved).\n92\t- Given the workspace store unreachable, artifact requests are denied with HTTP 503\n93\t  indicating workspace validation is unavailable (fail-closed).\n94\t- Startup with workspace-aware artifacts-only mode and no explicit `--workspace-store-uri`\n95\t  fails with a clear error.\n96\t- Every failure mode in the failure-mode to response matrix denies the request; no code\n97\t  path serves an artifact when workspace validation is active but incomplete.\n98\t- Workspace access denials are recorded in server logs with enough context to audit.\n99\t- Per-request latency overhead of workspace validation is measured and reported against the\n100\t  target agreed with PM/Engineering; where the target is exceeded, short-TTL caching of\n101\t  workspace membership decisions is implemented.\n102\t- Rollback / feature flag: workspace-aware artifact serving activates only when both\n103\t  `--artifacts-only` and `--enable-workspaces` are set; removing either flag restores the\n104\t  prior artifacts-only behavior with no residual enforcement path.\n105\t- Single-tenant deployments and configurations without workspace flags show no behavior\n106\t  change (regression).\n107\t\n108\t## HLR Traceability\n109\t\n110\t- HLR-1 (P0): `--artifacts-only` combinable with `--enable-workspaces` and\n111\t  `--workspace-store-uri` for workspace-validated artifact serving.\n112\t- HLR-2 (P0): artifact requests validated against workspace membership; non-members denied\n113\t  with HTTP 403.\n114\t- HLR-3 (P0): fail-closed behavior when the workspace store is unreachable.\n115\t- HLR-4 (P0): single-tenant and non-workspace deployments retain current behavior.\n116\t- HLR-8 (P2) — bundled into this epic: audit logging of workspace access denials through\n117\t  server logs is emitted at the same denial sites HLR-2 implements, in the same\n118\t  request-handling code; a separate epic would modify the same files twice, so the P2 work\n119\t  is not independently schedulable.\n120\t\n121\t## Risks / Notes\n122\t\n123\t- The error-handling acceptance criteria adopt the failure-mode to response matrix from the\n124\t  fail-mode analysis; the path-resolution and hardening requirements adopt the security\n125\t  bypass analysis findings.\n126\t- No latency target is specified in the RFE or architecture context (open question owned by\n127\t  PM/Engineering); the measure-then-optimize acceptance criterion above is the mitigation.\n128\t- Workspace resolution capability in the artifacts-only context is delivered by the\n129\t  `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` workspace resolution work; this epic builds against it.\n130\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-871f804eb52a36b1","agent_id":"aea88d3ef849ba58d","session_id":"36784e31-2123-4326-9e59-f3bb80327bfe","uuid":"86701e3d-93fb-4dbd-82b1-58f3e7ff19b2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:46:21.825Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcc981061f6587ae","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
