{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aeacdd4b69525ae8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E009\n3\ttitle: Main tracking server artifact-traffic delegation configuration (conditional\n4\t  branch B)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tbranch: B\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If ingress-level routing is sufficient (outcome A), this epic\n17\t    is removed; artifact traffic routing is handled entirely by the operator's HTTPRoute\n18\t    configuration for the dedicated artifacts-only instance, with no change to the\n19\t    main tracking server.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 0\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: 0\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: Medium\n33\tai_implementability_score: 2\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Main tracking server artifact-traffic delegation configuration (conditional branch B)\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tConditional branch of the decomposition — this epic exists only if the artifact traffic\n41\trouting design investigation determines that the main tracking server needs a configuration\n42\tchange to delegate artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance (outcome B).\n43\tIt delivers that main-tracking-server-side delegation configuration so that artifact\n44\toperations requested through the main tracking deployment are served by the dedicated\n45\tartifacts-only instance with workspace validation preserved end-to-end. If the\n46\tinvestigation selects outcome A (ingress-level routing suffices), this epic is removed and\n47\tartifact traffic routing is handled entirely by the operator's routing configuration.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Implement the main-tracking-server-side artifact delegation configuration selected by the\n52\t  routing design decision, at the functional level the decision defines (the mechanism is\n53\t  determined by the routing design investigation, not prescribed here).\n54\t- Ensure the delegation applies only when split-server artifact serving is enabled;\n55\t  deployments without it retain current artifact-serving behavior on the main tracking\n56\t  deployment.\n57\t- Verify end-to-end that artifact requests entering the main tracking deployment are\n58\t  delegated to the dedicated artifacts-only instance and that workspace validation is\n59\t  enforced on the delegated path (no bypass through the delegation).\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- With split-server artifact serving enabled, artifact operations requested via the main\n64\t  tracking deployment are served by the dedicated artifacts-only instance, verified\n65\t  end-to-end with workspace validation enforced (member allowed, non-member denied).\n66\t- With split-server artifact serving disabled, the main tracking deployment serves\n67\t  artifacts exactly as before (no delegation active; backwards compatible).\n68\t- The implemented configuration follows the routing design decision's recommended\n69\t  approach.\n70\t- No existing API contract, CLI argument, or configuration key is removed or changed in\n71\t  meaning.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n76\t  artifacts-only instance — the server-side portion of this HLR, required only under\n77\t  routing outcome B.\n78\t\n79\t## Risks / Notes\n80\t\n81\t- This epic is gated by the artifact traffic routing design investigation and is removed if\n82\t  that investigation selects ingress-level routing (outcome A).\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-871f804eb52a36b1","agent_id":"aea88d3ef849ba58d","session_id":"36784e31-2123-4326-9e59-f3bb80327bfe","uuid":"a67c60aa-0232-4c0c-93cd-ff88faadb9aa","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:46:24.094Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aeacdd4b69525ae8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
