{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f6bbe72ac623669","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-8009\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: Type Correctness\n9\t  description: 'E005 gate_failure_impact.fallback_approach records only the E001 coupling/rewrite\n10\t    gate; the decomposition summary DAG Justification declares the E002->E005 edge\n11\t    a true gate with action add_remediation (plugin-side resolution hardening for\n12\t    unresolvable/ambiguous paths), but that remediation branch is absent from E005\n13\t    gate metadata (E006 and E007 encode their security/fail-mode remediation branches\n14\t    in their fallback_approach text). Correction: extend E005 fallback_approach to\n15\t    name the security-remediation branch.'\n16\terror: null\n17\t---\n18\t## Review Summary\n19\t\n20\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n21\tRecommendation: accept\n22\t\n23\tContract validator: OK (`validate_decomposition.py RHAISTRAT-8009` exits 0). Triage\n24\tconsistency: `triage: null` (full decomposition) with 8 main-plan epics plus 1 conditional\n25\tbranch — no triage contradiction. All 7 criteria score 2/2; one minor issue recorded\n26\t(criterion 4, gate-metadata completeness on E005). No critical or major issues found.\n27\t\n28\t## Criterion Details\n29\t\n30\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n31\t\n32\tAll 8 HLRs map to at least one epic: HLR-1 through HLR-4 (P0) → E006 (server), HLR-5/HLR-6\n33\t(P1) → E007 (+ BRANCH-B-E009 under routing outcome B), HLR-7 (P1) → E005, HLR-8 (P2) → E006.\n34\tThe traceability matrix is present and complete; every row is corroborated by the named\n35\tepic's own HLR Traceability section.\n36\t\n37\tPriority inheritance is correct: E005 is P0 by inheritance (its own HLR-7 is P1, but it is\n38\ta build-against prerequisite of the P0 server epic and blocks all P0 work); E001/E002/E003\n39\tare P0 investigations blocking