{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b33bedb3d114e045","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: Extend mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If workspace resolution is coupled to the full tracking server\n17\t    initialization path, the plugin refactors workspace resolution into an independent\n18\t    initialization path within this epic; if resolution proves infeasible without\n19\t    tracking stores, the server-side validation design is rewritten before implementation\n20\t    proceeds.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: -1\n27\t  external_dependency: 0\n28\t  human_process_gates: 0\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: High\n34\tai_implementability_score: 5\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\tbranch: null\n37\t---\n38\t# Extend mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only context\n39\t\n40\t## Description\n41\t\n42\tMakes the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin's workspace resolution function correctly\n43\tin the MLflow artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores\n44\tare not initialized. Depending on the outcome of the workspace-resolution dependency\n45\tinvestigation, this is verification and extension of the existing resolution, or a\n46\trefactoring of workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the\n47\tplugin. The plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking\n48\tserver's non-artifact operations; this epic extends that capability to the artifacts-only\n49\tproxy context.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Verify and, where needed, extend the plugin's workspace resolution so it initializes and\n54\t  resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping without tracking store or model registry store\n55\t  initialization.\n56\t- If the workspace-resolution dependency investigation finds coupling to the full tracking\n57\t  server initialization path: factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization\n58\t  path within the plugin, preserving existing behavior for the full tracking server.\n59\t- Apply the path-resolution and resolution-hardening requirements from the security bypass\n60\t  analysis: unresolvable or ambiguous artifact paths must produce a deniable outcome, never\n61\t  a silent or wrong-workspace mapping.\n62\t- Preserve the existing registration mechanism (the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point\n63\t  group loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) and the existing behavior for the tracking\n64\t  server's non-artifact operations — changes to workspace isolation for non-artifact\n65\t  operations are out of scope per the strategy.\n66\t- Workspace authorization continues to reuse the existing auth plugin infrastructure; the\n67\t  kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup are unchanged. Per Staff\n68\t  Engineer input, Kubernetes API mechanics are implementation details and are not prescribed\n69\t  at strategy level.\n70\t\n71\t## Acceptance Criteria\n72\t\n73\t- The plugin's workspace resolution initializes in a server context where tracking and model\n74\t  registry stores are not initialized, demonstrated by a test reproducing the artifacts-only\n75\t  initialization.\n76\t- Experiment-to-workspace resolution returns correct mappings for resolvable artifact paths\n77\t  and a safe denial outcome for unresolvable or malformed paths, per the security analysis\n78\t  requirements.\n79\t- The tracking server's existing non-artifact workspace resolution behavior is unchanged\n80\t  (regression check).\n81\t- No new server flag, CR field, or changed CLI argument is introduced by this work (Staff\n82\t  Engineer input: no `--artifacts-only-workspace-aware` flag or equivalent).\n83\t\n84\t## HLR Traceability\n85\t\n86\t- HLR-7 (P1): Auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only\n87\t  context without tracking store initialization.\n88\t\n89\t## Risks / Notes\n90\t\n91\t- Approach (verify-and-extend vs. refactor) is determined by the workspace-resolution\n92\t  dependency investigation; if coupled, the refactoring is within this epic's scope.\n93\t- The plugin has no dedicated architecture-context file; it is documented indirectly by the\n94\t  MLflow architecture context as the external `kubernetes-auth` plugin package (v1.5.0).\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3b385cf10fb710d","agent_id":"a1cab434cbe8946aa","session_id":"36784e31-2123-4326-9e59-f3bb80327bfe","uuid":"8158853e-048a-4934-b356-d85b6da029c5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:54:37.644Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b33bedb3d114e045","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
