{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95f175408ce0c7a3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n3\ttitle: Determine artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Determine artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tInvestigation resolving the strategy's open question: how the operator should configure\n30\tartifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only\n31\tinstance. The answer affects the HTTPRoute design and determines whether the main tracking\n32\tserver needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations — which in turn\n33\tdetermines whether additional server-side work exists beyond the main plan.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Evaluate the candidate routing approaches at a functional level:\n38\t  - Ingress-level routing: Gateway API HTTPRoute configuration routes artifact traffic to\n39\t    the dedicated artifacts-only instance, with no change to the main tracking server.\n40\t  - Server-side delegation: the main tracking server is configured to delegate artifact\n41\t    operations to the dedicated instance.\n42\t  - A combination of both, if the analysis shows either alone is insufficient.\n43\t- For each candidate, assess feasibility against the operator's existing patterns — the\n44\t  Helm-in-operator rendering with server-side apply, and conditional Gateway API HTTPRoute\n45\t  creation based on runtime CRD discovery — and the operational surface of the split\n46\t  topology (two Deployments, two Services, two HTTPRoutes).\n47\t- Assess the impact on the main tracking deployment for each candidate, including\n48\t  backwards compatibility when split-server artifact serving is not enabled.\n49\t- Recommend one approach with rationale, identify exactly what changes in the operator, and\n50\t  state explicitly whether any main-tracking-server configuration change is required.\n51\t- Deliverable: a routing design decision document with bounded outcomes — (A) ingress-level\n52\t  routing suffices with no server change, or (B) server-side delegation configuration is\n53\t  required.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The decision document evaluates the candidate approaches and recommends one, with\n58\t  feasibility evidence grounded in the operator's existing rendering and routing patterns.\n59\t- The document states explicitly which bounded outcome holds — (A) ingress-level routing\n60\t  suffices, or (B) the main tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate\n61\t  artifact operations — since this selects the conditional branch of the decomposition.\n62\t- The HTTPRoute design implications for the dedicated artifacts-only instance are described\n63\t  at a functional level sufficient to implement the operator's routing configuration.\n64\t- Backwards compatibility is addressed: deployments that do not enable split-server\n65\t  artifact serving are unaffected by the chosen design.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\tInvestigation epic — no HLR ownership. De-risks HLR-6 and determines whether additional\n70\tmain-tracking-server delegation work exists (conditional branch of the decomposition).\n71\t\n72\t## Risks / Notes\n73\t\n74\t- Owner per the strategy's open questions table: MLflow Team.\n75\t- The strategy's risk table flags split-deployment operational complexity: misconfiguration\n76\t  could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation. The chosen design must compose\n77\t  with the operator validation that rejects configurations where the artifacts-only instance\n78\t  lacks workspace flags.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80108d2f7311d22b","agent_id":"a3efa4e901997f78f","session_id":"36784e31-2123-4326-9e59-f3bb80327bfe","uuid":"4e6e7cd2-a7e4-4f5f-889a-8a670a33d1cd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:55:45.550Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-95f175408ce0c7a3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
