{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-972e8a376113531d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E007\n3\ttitle: MLflow operator split-server topology for workspace-aware artifact serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design selects server-side delegation rather than\n16\t    ingress-level routing, the operator's routing configuration is rewritten per the\n17\t    selected design and the main-tracking-server delegation work is planned in the\n18\t    decomposition's conditional branch; security findings may add configuration-validation\n19\t    remediation.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: 0\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 5\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# MLflow operator split-server topology for workspace-aware artifact serving\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tExtends the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a\n42\tseparate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — a split-server topology — and to\n43\tconfigure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated\n44\tinstance. This is a split deployment, not a single-deployment configuration toggle (Staff\n45\tEngineer input). The operator propagates workspace configuration to the artifacts-only\n46\tinstance using the same configuration mechanisms it already uses for the main tracking\n47\tdeployment.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- New Helm chart templates within the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (MLflow\n52\t  CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, applied via\n53\t  server-side apply) for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute.\n54\t- Configuration of the main tracking deployment's artifact traffic routing to the dedicated\n55\t  instance, per the mechanism selected by the artifact traffic routing design investigation\n56\t  (ingress-level routing vs. server-side delegation; not prescribed here).\n57\t- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`,\n58\t  `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration\n59\t  mechanisms as the main tracking deployment; the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar is deployed on the\n60\t  artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment.\n61\t- Gateway API HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance created conditionally\n62\t  based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for\n63\t  optional dependencies.\n64\t- Operator validation that rejects split-server configurations where the artifacts-only\n65\t  instance would lack workspace flags, so misconfiguration cannot result in artifact\n66\t  requests bypassing workspace validation (strategy risk mitigation; requirements refined\n67\t  by the security bypass analysis).\n68\t- The split-server topology is opt-in: deployments that do not enable it retain the current\n69\t  single-deployment topology (rollback path).\n70\t- Verification that the operator's Helm chart rendering supports the additional Deployment\n71\t  for the artifacts-only instance without structural changes to the chart architecture\n72\t  (strategy assumption validated during implementation).\n73\t\n74\t## Acceptance Criteria\n75\t\n76\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciliation creates a\n77\t  dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main\n78\t  tracking Deployment, measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the\n79\t  correct flag combinations.\n80\t- The dedicated artifacts-only Deployment's container command runs with `--artifacts-only\n81\t  --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth\n82\t  --serve-artifacts`, verified by inspecting the rendered Deployment spec.\n83\t- Artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment is routed to the dedicated\n84\t  artifacts-only instance per the selected routing design, verified end-to-end.\n85\t- The operator rejects split-server configurations where the artifacts-only instance would\n86\t  lack workspace flags, with a clear validation error.\n87\t- Deployments that do not enable split-server artifact serving reconcile identically to\n88\t  current behavior (no additional resources created; backwards compatible), providing the\n89\t  rollback path.\n90\t- Workspace configuration propagation to the artifacts-only instance uses the same\n91\t  mechanisms as the main tracking deployment.\n92\t\n93\t## HLR Traceability\n94\t\n95\t- HLR-5 (P1): operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment\n96\t  with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n97\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n98\t  artifacts-only instance. (If the routing design investigation selects server-side\n99\t  delegation, the main-tracking-server portion of this HLR is planned in the conditional\n100\t  branch of the decomposition.)\n101\t\n102\t## Risks / Notes\n103\t\n104\t- The flag combination above requires the server-side flag composability delivered by the\n105\t  workspace-aware artifacts-only serving work in the MLflow tracking server. This is a\n106\t  configuration reference, not a build-against dependency: the operator templates are\n107\t  developed in parallel, and the coupling is enforced by the rendered Deployment\n108\t  verification above, never by a scheduling dependency.\n109\t- Strategy assumption to validate during implementation: the Helm chart rendering supports\n110\t  a second Deployment without structural changes to the chart architecture.\n111\t- No new CR field semantics beyond what the strategy states; per Staff Engineer input, no\n112\t  `spec.artifactsOnly.workspaceAware` field is introduced.\n113\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80108d2f7311d22b","agent_id":"a3efa4e901997f78f","session_id":"36784e31-2123-4326-9e59-f3bb80327bfe","uuid":"3f126bd8-cea2-414e-80ca-39dcb9456b57","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:55:49.636Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-972e8a376113531d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
