{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7c0bbaf186f9422","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E008\n3\ttitle: Integration validation of workspace-aware artifact serving across the split-server\n4\t  topology\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E007\n14\tai_signals:\n15\t  change_specificity: 1\n16\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n17\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n18\t  existing_foundation: 0\n19\t  open_questions: 0\n20\t  external_dependency: 0\n21\t  human_process_gates: 0\n22\t  repo_access: 1\n23\t  architecture_claims: 1\n24\timplementation_type: null\n25\tinvestigation_signals: null\n26\tai_implementability: High\n27\tai_implementability_score: 3\n28\tjira_key: null\n29\tbranch: null\n30\tgated_by: null\n31\tgate_failure_impact: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Integration validation of workspace-aware artifact serving across the split-server topology\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tCross-component integration and regression validation of the strategy's scenarios once the\n38\tserver, plugin, and operator work has landed, corresponding to the strategy's integration\n39\ttesting budget: multi-tenant workspace scenarios, backwards compatibility and single-tenant\n40\tregression, fail-closed edge cases, and split-server routing. The strategy's acceptance\n41\tcriteria are end-to-end scenarios that span the deployed split-server topology, so they are\n42\tverified here against the integrated system in addition to the per-epic acceptance\n43\tcriteria.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- End-to-end multi-tenant scenarios through the deployed split-server topology: a workspace\n48\t  member is served artifacts of their workspace's experiments (HTTP 200 with correct\n49\t  content); a non-member is denied (HTTP 403 with an insufficient-permissions error).\n50\t- Fail-closed edge cases as deployed: workspace store unreachable yields HTTP 503\n51\t  indicating workspace validation is unavailable, and every failure mode from the\n52\t  failure-mode to response matrix denies rather than serves.\n53\t- Single-tenant and non-workspace deployment regression: deployments without\n54\t  `--enable-workspaces` retain current artifacts-only behavior.\n55\t- Split-server routing verification: artifact traffic reaches the dedicated artifacts-only\n56\t  instance; experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry operations remain on\n57\t  the main tracking deployment.\n58\t- Backwards compatibility of existing API contracts, CLI arguments, and configuration keys\n59\t  (strategy Non-Functional Requirement).\n60\t- Reuse of the operator's existing test harness patterns where applicable, extending them\n61\t  to the multi-tenant workspace scenarios.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- The strategy's acceptance scenarios pass against the deployed split-server topology:\n66\t  member allowed (HTTP 200, correct content), non-member denied (HTTP 403),\n67\t  non-workspace-flagged deployment unchanged, workspace store unreachable denied (HTTP 503),\n68\t  dedicated artifacts-only Deployment/Service/HTTPRoute present with the correct flag\n69\t  combination, and artifact traffic routed to the dedicated instance. Results are recorded.\n70\t- The regression suite shows no behavior change for deployments without\n71\t  `--enable-workspaces` and for single-tenant deployments.\n72\t- All fail-closed edge cases from the failure-mode to response matrix pass as deployed.\n73\t- Existing API contracts, CLI arguments, and configuration keys behave identically to\n74\t  pre-strategy deployments (backwards compatibility check).\n75\t- Results are recorded with enough detail to support the strategy's acceptance sign-off.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\tVerification coverage (no sole HLR ownership): HLR-1 through HLR-6 are verified end-to-end\n80\there; primary implementation ownership rests with the server and operator implementation\n81\tepics. HLR-7 is verified within the plugin epic's own tests and exercised end-to-end by the\n82\tmulti-tenant scenarios above. HLR-8 (audit logging) is verified by inspecting server logs\n83\tfor the recorded denial scenarios.\n84\t\n85\t## Risks / Notes\n86\t\n87\t- Requires a deployed environment with the split-server topology, Gateway API routing, and\n88\t  a multi-tenant workspace configuration; scenario setup is part of this epic's work.\n89\t- If the routing design selects server-side delegation, the conditional branch's\n90\t  delegation configuration is verified as part of the split-server routing scenarios above.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80108d2f7311d22b","agent_id":"a3efa4e901997f78f","session_id":"36784e31-2123-4326-9e59-f3bb80327bfe","uuid":"15f2eca4-64a8-425c-9e15-59f078ffdcbd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:55:50.276Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7c0bbaf186f9422","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
